From 4529a1235690565f68a7d5d2eb978d14882c4bb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:35:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Annotate the remaining public C++ API with ONNX_API

With the shared ONNX libraries built with hidden visibility, and on
Windows exporting only ONNX_API symbols, separate consumers failed to
link against public helpers that were not annotated.

onnx_cpp2py_export needed the checker free functions, the inliner entry
points, OpSchema::Verify, the shape-inference helpers in
shape_inference/implementation.h and the proto streaming operators in
printer.h.

onnxruntime additionally needs (undefined references when linking
libonnxruntime, onnx_test_runner, onnxruntime_test_all and
onnxruntime_provider_test on linux, osx and Windows):

- the OpSchema::Attr overloads that take a default value, for every type
  instantiated by ATTR_SETTER_WITH_DEFAULT_VALUE plus const char*;
- OpSchemaRegistry::loaded_schema_version, read by inline accessors;
- ReplaceAll;
- the public DataTypeUtils static helpers;
- MatMulShapeInference, QLinearMatMulShapeInference and QLinearMatMulDoc;
- the mergeInShapeInfo and UnionShapeInfo overloads;
- both shape_inference::InferShapeForFunctionNode overloads;
- the ParseData template, whose instantiations live in the library.

The ToTensor and ParseData specializations are defined in
tensor_proto_util.cc and tensor_util.cc. GCC and clang give an explicit
specialization the visibility of its primary template, but MSVC only
exports it when the definition itself is dllexport, so onnx.dll exported
none of them and onnxruntime_conda.dll failed to link against
ParseData<int>, ParseData<int64_t> and ToTensor<int64_t>. Annotate the
definitions, and the ParseData(const Tensor*) declaration, with ONNX_API.

The exception classes InferenceError, SchemaError, ValidationError and
ConvertError are exported as whole classes too. They are defined inline
in the headers, so with hidden visibility every library gets its own
local typeinfo. GCC's runtime matches exception types by name, but on
macOS a `catch (const onnx::InferenceError&)` in onnxruntime does not
match an InferenceError thrown inside libonnx. Shape-inference errors that
onnxruntime tolerates or rewraps then escape: on osx-arm64, 27 of
onnxruntime's own unit tests failed, e.g. models that should load with a
shape warning fail with "[ShapeInferenceError] Mismatch between number of
inferred and declared dimensions". SchemaError's member annotations move
to the class.

GraphInferencerImpl is exported as a whole class so its vtable is
available to onnx_cpp2py_export, which instantiates it; MSVC forbids
dllexport on members of a dllexport class, so doInferencing loses its
own annotation.
